00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:06,420
So if you just try to run the math backwards, the system will freak out because it doesn't know which mountain range is the real one.

512
00:30:06,580 --> 00:30:07,800
You have to filter out the noise.

513
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:14,840
And that is exactly where singular value decomposition, or SVD, and Tikhanov regularization come into play.

514
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:20,260
SVD is a way of breaking down the mathematical operator into its fundamental frequencies.

515
00:30:20,260 --> 00:30:21,480
Like breaking down a wave.

516
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,160
Exactly.

517
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:23,980
Imagine the mountain range.

518
00:30:24,580 --> 00:30:29,060
The large singular values correspond to the massive, obvious features.

519
00:30:29,460 --> 00:30:30,660
The giant peaks.

520
00:30:31,140 --> 00:30:32,320
The deep canyons.

521
00:30:32,740 --> 00:30:36,880
The small singular values correspond to the tiny, fine-scale features.

522
00:30:37,120 --> 00:30:39,040
Like a single pebble on a hiking trail.

523
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:40,520
Or a small divot in the dirt.

524
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:44,840
Those tiny features got totally smeared out and obliterated in the projection.

525
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:55,080
So if you try to forcefully mathematically reconstruct the tiny pebbles from a blurry shadow, you are just going to end up amplifying the noise of the system and drawing a mountain that doesn't exist.

526
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:57,460
Which is why we use Tikhanov regularization.

527
00:30:58,040 --> 00:31:01,380
Think of it like a highly skilled audio engineer filtering a recording.

528
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:06,640
If you record something in a noisy room, there is a low-level hum of the air conditioner in the background.

529
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:07,920
Yeah, you don't want to turn that up.

530
00:31:08,140 --> 00:31:12,820
If you just crank up the overall volume to hear the voices better, the hum becomes deafening.

531
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:19,660
Tikhanov regularization is a mathematical filter that smoothly suppresses those small, singular values.

532
00:31:20,100 --> 00:31:22,100
So it's actively dampening the noise.

533
00:31:22,380 --> 00:31:23,760
It essentially tells the system,

534
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:34,620
We know we can't reliably reconstruct the tiny pebbles, so we're going to dampen those specific signals to ensure we get a crystal clear, accurate reconstruction of the massive peaks and valleys.

535
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:36,120
Okay, that makes perfect sense.

